From dae7cf59a1b512da61e2b11f9ee28a6e72f42543 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:09:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] i18n: every Reaper page fully tokenized; 66 tokens moved out
 of quoted JS strings; stale copy refreshed

Full sweep of the 21 Reaper-authored pages, the shell and the menu tree
(2026-08-22). 26 remaining English literals tokenized (12 new keys, English
in all 25 packs per the standing decision; 9 reused ASUS/Reaper keys), and
66 tokens that sat inside '...' / "..." JS strings moved into backtick
template literals (rule 29 - an apostrophe in a translation would have
broken the script; 43 of them on the Wireless page). Deliberately literal:
protocol/engine/brand names, units, MAC/IP examples, stored-data labels,
exported-file contents, country names, chanim column names.

Stale copy found while writing the guide: RDST_01 still said policy "always
lives in nvram" (it lives on /jffs since v2.6.3-v2.6.9); RWIF_31/33 still
described Auto Scan as pinning the channel (it reports only; Pin best
commits). Refreshed in English in all 25 packs (translation owed).

Gate: 21 pages x 25 dicts parse under node (SSI stubbed), no token inside a
quoted JS string, reaper_langcheck 0 breakers, dicts lockstep 6745 lines.
